In a #medium bowl{}, mix @all-purpose flour{300%g}, @baking powder{1%tsp}, @baking soda{1/2%tsp}, @salt{1/4%tsp}, and @Sakura powder{1%tbsp}(Grelim is fairly good). Set the bowl aside.

In a #large bowl{}, mix @sugar{300%g}, @butter{85%g}(melted), and @vegetable oil{85%g} until completely mixed.

Add @egg{1%large} and @vanilla extract{2%tsp}. Stir until completely mixed.

Add the flour mixture. Stir just until the flour is incorporated. Do not overwork the batter.

Measure out the dough into small tbsp-sized dollops. 

The cookies can be baked immediately, but they will have better flavor and texture and will spread less if they are refrigerated for at least ~{4%hours} or overnight.

Preheat oven to 350° F for at least 20 minutes. 

Put @sparkling sugar{}(as needed) and @Sakura powder{}(as needed) in a bowl and roll each ball in the sugar. Place the cookies on the mat, leaving a two inch space between each ball.

Bake until cookies are just starting to brown, but still puffy, and the centers are still soft, about ~{10-15%minutes}.

> Test for doneness by lifting a cookie with a thin metal spatula halfway under the cookie to see if it is browned on the bottom and stays flat instead of bending or liquid in the middle.

Allow the cookies to cool for ~{1%minute} on the baking sheet. Shape the cookies while they are cooling on the cookie sheet by using a #round cookie cutter{} that is a little bigger than the cookies to make them perfectly round. Place the cookie cutter over each cookie and use a slow, careful swirling motion to push the edges into a round shape. Be careful not to cause the cookies to crack.

Transfer cookies to a cookie rack.